): the archive becomes collab/ — one version-controlled collaboration root\\nad8e3a9c fix(jolt-parser): free the full-context reach set on the exception path (J5c, the P3 leak)\\ndf6abeb9 merge: origin/master — the yang.call S1 TS wiring reconciled with the T3 class machinery\\n     1\\t(ns yang.call.conformance\\n     2\\t  \\\"The cross-language calling gates' shared composition (docs/design/\\n     3\\t   yang.antlr.md section 8.10.11): a donor program's named export reaches a\\n     4\\t   caller program by explicit published-export composition only.\\n     5\\t\\n     6\\t   A donor is real source of any admitted frontend, lowered unmodified and\\n     7\\t   published as an ordinary linker module whose one export, `body`, is the\\n     8\\t   lowered unit. A caller task requires that module, runs its body under the\\n     9\\t   donor runtime's own entry (`js/run-main`, `php/run-main`), reads each\\n    10\\t   named export from the donor runtime's global namespace, and projects it\\n    11\\t   into the caller runtime's namespace under the same name; then the caller\\n    12\\t   source, lowered unmodified, runs under its own entry. The composition is\\n    13\\t   a sequence of top-level nodes: no call node is rewritten, no foreign\\n    14\\t   `:code` is extracted, no language-pair wrapper is inserted, and the\\n    15\\t   projected value is the donor's own function cell (identity survives).\\n    16\\t\\n    17\\t   A callable value is task-local (a function is a cell, and cells are\\n    18\\t   task-local, section 8.11), so the export is answered as a node evaluated\\n    19\\t   in the caller's task, never as a host value carried between tasks.\\n    20\\t   `export-program` answers the donor's export alone as the program's value.\\n    21\\t\\n    22\\t   Every program runs linked on the three vector VMs (`semantic`, `stack`,\\n    23\\t   `register`) over the TypeScript linked harness's content store, where\\n    24\\t   `yang.call` and `js` already live and `php` is published beside them.\\n    25\\t   The AST walker is not a backend: its links are refused until L-b.\\\"\\n    26\\t  (:require\\n    27\\t    [clojure.string :as str]\\n    28\\t    [yang.core.module :as core-module]\\n    29\\t    [yang.core.names :as names]\\n    30\\t    [yang.core.uast :as u]\\n    31\\t    [yang.php.antlr.cst :as php-cst]\\n    32\\t    [yang.php.antlr.lower :as php-lower]\\n    33\\t    [yang.php.antlr.portable-harness :as php-h]\\n    34\\t    [yang.php.antlr.prelude :as php-prelude]\\n    35\\t    [yang.python.antlr.lower :as py-lower]\\n    36\\t    [yang.python.antlr.parser :as py-parser]\\n    37\\t    [yang.python.antlr.prelude :as py-prelude]\\n    38\\t    [yang.python.antlr.render :as py-render]\\n    39\\t    [yang.typescript.antlr.cst :as ts-cst]\\n    40\\t    [yang.typescript.antlr.linked-harness :as h]\\n    41\\t    [yang.typescript.antlr.lower :as ts-lower]\\n    42\\t    [yang.typescript.antlr.render :as render]\\n    43\\t    [yin.vm :as vm]))\\n    44\\t\\n    45\\t\\n    46\\t(def ^:private published-php\\n    47\\t  \\\"`php` published once into `js`'s content store, pinning the same\\n    48\\t   `yang.call` revision (as `source-call-test` publishes it).\\\"\\n    49\\t  (delay (h/publish-guest-module!\\n    50\\t           (php-prelude/module-spec (h/registry)\\n    51\\t                                    (:call-address @h/published)))))\\n    52\\t\\n    53\\t\\n    54\\t(def ^:private published-py\\n    55\\t  \\\"`py` published beside `js` and `php`, over the same host registry and\\n    56\\t   `yang.call` revision.\\\"\\n    57\\t  (delay (h/publish-guest-module!\\n    58\\t           (py-prelude/module-spec (h/registry)\\n    59\\t                                   (:call-address @h/published)))))\\n    60\\t\\n    61\\t\\n    62\\t(defn- parse-ok\\n    63\\t  \\\"The CST packet of `source` under `parse`, refused unless the parse is ok.\\\"\\n    64\\t  [parse source]\\n    65\\t  (let [pk (parse source)]\\n    66\\t    (when-not (= :yang.cst/ok (:yang.cst/outcome pk))\\n    67\\t      (throw (ex-info \\\"donor or caller source does not parse\\\"\\n    68\\t                      {:source source, :packet (dissoc pk :yang.cst/nodes)})))\\n    69\\t    pk))\\n    70\\t\\n    71\\t\\n    72\\t(defn- python-export-symbol\\n    73\\t  [export]\\n    74\\t  (symbol (str \\\"xlang.python.export.\\\" export)))\\n    75\\t\\n    76\\t\\n    77\\t(defn- python-unit\\n    78\\t  [packet exports]\\n    79\\t  (u/lam [py-lower/globals-sym py-lower/globals-fn-sym]\\n    80\\t         (u/seq-nodes\\n    81\\t           (concat (map (fn [export]\\n    82\\t                          (u/sexp->uast\\n    83\\t                            (list 'py/global-set py-lower/globals-sym\\n    84\\t                                  {:py/str export} (python-export-symbol export))))\\n    85\\t                        exports)\\n    86\\t                   [(py-lower/lower-module-body packet)]))))\\n    87\\t\\n    88\\t\\n    89\\t(def frontends\\n    90\\t  \\\"Each admitted frontend's profile, as data:\\n    91\\t\\n    92\\t   - `:runtime`, `:address`: the runtime module and its published address;\\n    93\\t   - `:refusal`: the publication refusal key and reason of its modules;\\n    94\\t   - `:parse`: source text to CST packet;\\n    95\\t   - `:unit`: packet and projected exports to the lowered unit its\\n    96\\t     `:run-main` entry takes;\\n    97\\t   - `:read-export`: export name to the form reading the runtime's global\\n    98\\t     namespace (JS `globalThis`, PHP's named-function table, Python's main\\n    99\\t     module dictionary);\\n   100\\t   - `:project`: name and a value form to the form binding the value where\\n   101\\t     the runtime's source resolves a called name;\\n   102\\t   - `:render`: the `:run-main` value as test data.\\\"\\n   103\\t  {:typescript\\n   104\\t   {:runtime 'js,\\n   105\\t    :address #(:address @h/published),\\n   106\\t    :refusal [:yang.typescript.antlr/refusal :yang.typescript.antlr/undeclared-free],\\n   107\\t    :parse #(parse-ok ts-cst/parse-source %),\\n   108\\t    :unit (fn [packet _] (names/canonicalize (ts-lower/lower-unit packet))),\\n   109\\t    :run-main 'js/run-main,\\n   110\\t    :read-export (fn [export] (list 'js/global-get {:js/str export})),\\n   111\\t    :project (fn [name value] (list 'js/define-global! name value)),\\n   112\\t    :render render/output},\\n   113\\t   :php\\n   114\\t   {:runtime 'php,\\n   115\\t    :address #(:address @published-php),\\n   116\\t    :refusal [:yang.php/refusal :yang.php/undeclared-free],\\n   117\\t    :parse #(parse-ok php-cst/parse-source %),\\n   118\\t    :unit (fn [packet _] (u/lam [] (php-lower/lower-module-body packet))),\\n   119\\t    :run-main 'php/run-main,\\n   120\\t    :read-export (fn [export]\\n   121\\t                   (list 'php/resolve-fn (str/lower-case export) export)),\\n   122\\t    :project (fn [name value]\\n   123\\t               (list 'php/declare-function! (str/lower-case name) value)),\\n   124\\t    :render php-h/render},\\n   125\\t   :python\\n   126\\t   {:runtime 'py,\\n   127\\t    :address #(:address @published-py),\\n   128\\t    :refusal [:yang.python.antlr/refusal :yang.python.antlr/undeclared-free],\\n   129\\t    :parse #(parse-ok py-parser/parse-source %),\\n   130\\t    :unit python-unit,\\n   131\\t    :run-main 'py/run-main,\\n   132\\t    :read-export (fn [export]\\n   133\\t                   (list 'py/global-get\\n   134\\t                         (list 'py/module-dict\\n   135\\t                               (list 'py/modules-ref {:py/str \\\"__main__\\\"}))\\n   136\\t                         {:py/str export})),\\n   137\\t    :project (fn [name value]\\n   138\\t               (list 'yin/def (list 'quote (python-export-symbol name)) value)),\\n   139\\t    :render py-render/output}})\\n   140\\t\\n   141\\t\\n   142\\t(defn- profile\\n   143\\t  [frontend]\\n   144\\t  (or (get frontends frontend)\\n   145\\t      (throw (ex-info \\\"frontend not admitted\\\" {:frontend frontend}))))\\n   146\\t\\n   147\\t\\n   148\\t(defn publish-donor!\\n   149\\t  \\\"Publish the donor `source` of `frontend` as the module `module` (default\\n   150\\t   `xlang.donor.<frontend>`), exporting `body`, its unmodified lowered unit.\\n   151\\t   Answers `{:frontend :module :address :links}`.\\\"\\n   152\\t  ([frontend source]\\n   153\\t   (publish-donor! frontend source (symbol (str \\\"xlang.donor.\\\" (name frontend)))))\\n   154\\t  ([frontend source module]\\n   155\\t   (let [{:keys [runtime address refusal parse unit]} (profile frontend)\\n   156\\t         [refusal-key reason] refusal\\n   157\\t         spec (core-module/module-spec\\n   158\\t                refusal-key reason (h/registry)\\n   159\\t                {:name module,\\n   160\\t                 :ast (core-module/module-tree\\n   161\\t                        [(core-module/require-node runtime)\\n   162\\t                         (u/def! 'body (unit (parse source) []))]),\\n   163\\t                 :exports '#{body},\\n   164\\t                 :runtime-name runtime,\\n   165\\t                 :runtime-address (address)})\\n   166\\t         result (h/publish-guest-module! spec)]\\n   167\\t     {:frontend frontend,\\n   168\\t      :module module,\\n   169\\t      :address (:address result),\\n   170\\t      :links (:links result)})))\\n   171\\t\\n   172\\t\\n   173\\t(defn- runtime-entry\\n   174\\t  \\\"Require and initialize each distinct runtime of `frontend-keys`, once.\\\"\\n   175\\t  [frontend-keys]\\n   176\\t  (into [(core-module/require-node 'yang.call)]\\n   177\\t        (mapcat (fn [runtime]\\n   178\\t                  [(core-module/require-node runtime)\\n   179\\t                   (u/sexp->uast (list (symbol (str runtime) \\\"init!\\\")))]))\\n   180\\t        (distinct (map (comp :runtime profile) frontend-keys))))\\n   181\\t\\n   182\\t\\n   183\\t(defn- donor-run\\n   184\\t  \\\"The donor module required and its body run under its runtime's entry.\\\"\\n   185\\t  [{:keys [frontend module]}]\\n   186\\t  [(core-module/require-node module)\\n   187\\t   (u/app (u/v (:run-main (profile frontend)))\\n   188\\t          (u/v (symbol (str module) \\\"body\\\")))])\\n   189\\t\\n   190\\t\\n   191\\t(defn export-program\\n   192\\t  \\\"The program whose value is the donor's `export`, read from its runtime's\\n   193\\t   global namespace after its body ran.\\\"\\n   194\\t  [donor export]\\n   195\\t  (let [{:keys [read-export]} (profile (:frontend donor))]\\n   196\\t    (u/mark-tails\\n   197\\t      (u/seq-nodes (concat (runtime-entry [(:frontend donor)])\\n   198\\t                           (donor-run donor)\\n   199\\t                           [(u/sexp->uast (read-export export))])))))\\n   200\\t\\n   201\\t\\n   202\\t(defn compose\\n   203\\t  \\\"The caller program: the donor's body run, each name of `exports` read\\n   204\\t   from the donor runtime and projected into `caller-frontend`'s namespace\\n   205\\t   under the same name, then `caller-source`, lowered unmodified, run under\\n   206\\t   its runtime's entry. Its value is the caller entry's value.\\\"\\n   207\\t  [donor exports caller-frontend caller-source]\\n   208\\t  (let [{:keys [read-export]} (profile (:frontend donor))\\n   209\\t        {:keys [project parse unit run-main]} (profile caller-frontend)]\\n   210\\t    (u/mark-tails\\n     1\\t(ns yang.cross-lang-test\\n     2\\t  \\\"The substrate claim, empirically (yang.antlr.md 8.10/8.11): both preludes\\n     3\\t   bottom out in `:application`, and the engine neither knows nor cares which\\n     4\\t   frontend minted a closure. A TypeScript function value is called from\\n     5\\t   PHP-lowered code and a PHP closure from TypeScript-lowered code, in one\\n     6\\t   task, one run.\\n     7\\t\\n     8\\t   The seam is explicit published-export composition (8.10.11), owned by\\n     9\\t   `yang.call.conformance`: the donor source is published as a module and\\n    10\\t   run unmodified, its named export is read from the donor runtime's global\\n    11\\t   namespace (`globalThis.ts_fn`, PHP's `phpfn` function) and projected into the caller\\n    12\\t   runtime's namespace under the same name, and the caller source runs\\n    13\\t   unmodified. No call node is rewritten and no foreign `:code` extracted:\\n    14\\t   the caller holds the donor's own function cell, as the identity check\\n    15\\t   (`stored === phpfn`) shows.\\n    16\\t\\n    17\\t   What is pinned as LIMITS (documented expectations, not failures):\\n    18\\t   a PHP array reaching TypeScript is an opaque handle that only PHP can use;\\n    19\\t   PHP null (`:php/null`) is neither JS null nor undefined. Each case runs\\n    20\\t   linked on the three vector VMs, which must agree.\\\"\\n    21\\t  (:require\\n    22\\t    [clojure.test :refer [deftest is testing]]\\n    23\\t    [yang.call.conformance :as xl]))\\n    24\\t\\n    25\\t\\n    26\\t(deftest ts-closure-called-from-php-test\\n    27\\t  (testing \\\"a number crosses as a number: float in, float out\\\"\\n    28\\t    (is (= \\\"4\\\"\\n    29\\t           (xl/call [:typescript \\\"globalThis.ts_fn = (x, y) => x + y;\\\"]\\n    30\\t                    [\\\"ts_fn\\\"]\\n    31\\t                    [:php \\\"<?php echo ts_fn(1.5, 2.5);\\\"]))))\\n    32\\t  (testing \\\"the PHP caller sees the result as an ordinary value\\\"\\n    33\\t    (is (= \\\"yes\\\"\\n    34\\t           (xl/call [:typescript \\\"globalThis.ts_fn = (x, y) => x + y;\\\"]\\n    35\\t                    [\\\"ts_fn\\\"]\\n    36\\t                    [:php \\\"<?php echo ts_fn(1.5, 2.5) == 4 ? 'yes' : 'no';\\\"])))))\\n    37\\t\\n    38\\t\\n    39\\t(deftest php-closure-called-from-ts-test\\n    40\\t  (testing \\\"TS stores and calls the same PHP function cell it received\\\"\\n    41\\t    (is (= {:js/out [\\\"true 5\\\"], :js/uncaught nil}\\n    42\\t           (xl/call [:php \\\"<?php function phpfn($a, $b) { return $a + $b; }\\\"]\\n    43\\t                    [\\\"phpfn\\\"]\\n    44\\t                    [:typescript\\n    45\\t                     \\\"const stored = phpfn; console.log(stored === phpfn, stored(2, 3));\\\"])))))\\n    46\\t\\n    47\\t\\n    48\\t(deftest python-calls-typescript-closure-test\\n    49\\t  (testing \\\"TS stores and calls the same Python function cell it received\\\"\\n    50\\t    (is (= {:py/out [\\\"22\\\"], :py/exception nil}\\n    51\\t           (xl/call [:typescript\\n    52\\t                     (str \\\"globalThis.ts_apply = f => { globalThis.stored = f; \\\"\\n    53\\t                          \\\"return stored === f ? f(20n) + 1n : -1n; };\\\")]\\n    54\\t                    [\\\"ts_apply\\\"]\\n    55\\t                    [:python \\\"print(ts_apply(lambda x: x + 1))\\\\n\\\"])))))\\n    56\\t\\n    57\\t\\n    58\\t(deftest typescript-calls-python-closure-test\\n    59\\t  (testing \\\"Python stores and calls the same TS function cell it received\\\"\\n    60\\t    (is (= {:js/out [\\\"22n\\\"], :js/uncaught nil}\\n    61\\t           (xl/call [:python\\n    62\\t                     (str \\\"def py_apply(f):\\\\n\\\"\\n    63\\t                          \\\"    global stored\\\\n\\\"\\n    64\\t                          \\\"    stored = f\\\\n\\\"\\n    65\\t                          \\\"    return f(20) + 1 if stored is f else -1\\\")]\\n    66\\t                    [\\\"py_apply\\\"]\\n    67\\t                    [:typescript\\n    68\\t                     \\\"console.log(py_apply(x => x + 1n));\\\"])))))\\n    69\\t\\n    70\\t\\n    71\\t(deftest python-calls-php-closure-test\\n    72\\t  (testing \\\"PHP stores and calls the same Python function cell it received\\\"\\n    73\\t    (is (= {:py/out [\\\"22\\\"], :py/exception nil}\\n    74\\t           (xl/call [:php\\n    75\\t                     (str \\\"<?php function php_apply($f) 