{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_32","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"cat collab/orch-lane/1794260000000-engineer-p7a-budget.kimi-k3.1-pro.findings.md collab/orch-lane/1794290000000-engineer-p5-request-context.kimi-k3.1-pro.findings.md collab/orch-lane/1794350000000-engineer-p9-builtin-surfaces.kimi-k3.1-pro.findings.md collab/orch-lane/1794230000002-engineer-xlang-s2-kimi-findings-recovered.md; /Library/Developer/CommandLineTools/usr/bin/git show --format=short --stat d01a7c80; /Library/Developer/CommandLineTools/usr/bin/git show d01a7c80 -- docs/agents/known-gaps.md | head -85; sed -n '1,80p' docs/agents/known-gaps.md\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_32","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"cat collab/orch-lane/1794260000000-engineer-p7a-budget.kimi-k3.1-pro.findings.md collab/orch-lane/1794290000000-engineer-p5-request-context.kimi-k3.1-pro.findings.md collab/orch-lane/1794350000000-engineer-p9-builtin-surfaces.kimi-k3.1-pro.findings.md collab/orch-lane/1794230000002-engineer-xlang-s2-kimi-findings-recovered.md; /Library/Developer/CommandLineTools/usr/bin/git show --format=short --stat d01a7c80; /Library/Developer/CommandLineTools/usr/bin/git show d01a7c80 -- docs/agents/known-gaps.md | head -85; sed -n '1,80p' docs/agents/known-gaps.md\"","aggregated_output":"# P7-a guest execution budget findings\n\n## Delivered\n\nCommit `483ae0bc` (`feat(yang.php): the optional safepoint-count execution budget`) on `feat/p7a-exec-budget`; not pushed.\n\n- Added the bundled `phpsp` profile and optional per-run safepoint counter. Only existing PHP `:loop` and `:call` sites are charged; omission leaves the original AST and execution unchanged.\n- `:execution-budget` is available through the JVM `run-php` / `run-vms` harness.\n- Exhaustion unwinds past guest handlers, produces exactly `PHP Fatal error:  Maximum execution time of 30 seconds exceeded`, and bypasses uncaught-exception handling, shutdown functions, and destructors.\n- Extended shared safepoint insertion with an opt-in `:sequence` profile entry so PHP call-application sites can run an entry hook; existing profiles retain their previous behavior.\n- Documented the deterministic, non-wall-clock contract in `docs/design/yang.php.md` section 12.\n\n## Verification\n\n- Focused `yang.php.antlr.safepoint-test`: 2 tests, 9 assertions, 0 failures/errors. Covers exact fatal text on AST walker, semantic, stack, and register VMs; no guest catch/destructor output; default unbounded behavior; unexhausted-budget transparency.\n- `yang.safepoint-test`, `yang.php.antlr.class-model-test`, `yang.php.antlr.objects-test`, `yang.php.antlr.generators-test`: 22 tests, 1,218 assertions, 0 failures/errors.\n- `clj -X:fmt`: completed after trusting this checkout's `mise.toml`; unrelated formatter/generated-manifest changes were restored.\n- Focused clj-kondo over every changed Clojure source/test: 0 errors, 0 warnings.\n- `git diff --check`: clean before commit.\n\nGenerated parser classes were required for the standard PHP harness and were produced with `clj -M:antlr-gen`; generated files remain ignored/uncommitted. The findings file is intentionally uncommitted.\n# P5 request context findings\n\n## Delivered\n\n- Bound `$_GET`, `$_POST`, `$_COOKIE`, `$_SERVER`, `$_ENV`, `$_FILES`, and `$_REQUEST` from an explicit, task-local request record. Request collections accept either PHP arrays or ordered entry vectors; missing collections become empty arrays. `$_REQUEST` uses GET-then-POST replacement order.\n- Added output-buffer stack operations, ordered response records for headers/cookies/status/body, and headers-after-output diagnostics.\n- Lowered both `exit`/`die` parser forms to the runtime exit path. Exit runs shutdown functions, returns its status, and is not reported as an uncaught error.\n- Added user error triggering, handler restoration, `getenv`, and `php_sapi_name` registrations.\n- Added eight hand-derived P5 fixtures, all marked `:oracle :pending`, plus an independent-task isolation test using two separate VM sessions.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `clojure -M:test -n yang.php.antlr.request-context-test`: 3 tests, 35 assertions, all passing.\n- `clojure -M:test -n yang.php.antlr.class-model-test -n yang.php.antlr.objects-test -n yang.php.antlr.generators-test`: 14 tests, 1201 assertions, all passing.\n- `clojure -M:kondo --lint` over all changed Clojure files: 0 errors, 0 warnings.\n- Managed `cljstyle 0.17.642` check over all changed Clojure files: passing.\n- `git diff --check`: passing.\n\nNo PHP oracle recording was performed, as requested for this round. No push was performed.\n# P9 builtin surfaces — engineer findings\n\n## Landed\n\n- Strings II: substring/search/replacement, predicates, trimming, case, repeat/pad/reverse, comparisons, strstr/strrchr, substr_count, nl2br, basic HTML and slash escaping, byte/hex conversion.\n- Arrays II: explode/str_split, reverse/product/search/list checks, fill/fill_keys/combine/flip/pad/chunk/column/slice/splice/map/filter/reduce/unique/diff/intersect/range.\n- Math II: abs/ceil/floor/round/sqrt/pow/min/max/is_finite/is_infinite.\n- JSON: scalar/array/associative-array encoding and decoding, string escapes, pretty printing, and JSON_THROW_ON_ERROR.\n- Dynamic variables (`$$`), dictionary-backed extract/compact, `$GLOBALS` reads and element writes.\n- C5 in-range positive/negative string writes; C6 array_multisort refusal; C11 EXTR_REFS and dynamic-reference refusals; C12 nested destructuring-reference refusal; C13 whole-$GLOBALS refusals.\n- New `programs_p9.cljc` groups and `builtin_surfaces_test.clj`; all fixture outputs hand-derived and marked `:oracle :pending`.\n- Updated the stale G-str-offset-write design row.\n\n## Remaining P9 work\n\n- `eval` still needs the runtime compilation-request bridge. It is explicitly refused with `:yang.php/unsupported :eval`; no fake evaluator or undefined `php/eval` call remains.\n- JSON objects decoded without `$associative` currently use the same array representation rather than `stdClass`; object encoding and JsonSerializable are not implemented. Control-byte escaping and Unicode surrogate pairs need completion.\n- Uncovered catalogue entries include formatting (`sprintf`/`printf`/`vsprintf`, `number_format`, wordwrap/chunk_split), hashes/base conversions, recursive merge/walk, associative diff/intersect variants, iterator_to_array, and additional math functions.\n\n## Implementation notes\n\n- Prelude guest vectors containing expressions must be built with `php/vconj`; a raw quoted vector does not evaluate its elements.\n- The JSON decoder uses one rooted cell containing `[code-points index associative? throw?]`. Object parsing must consume the opening quote before reading a key.\n- String replacement bounds-checks its needle before substring reads. String offset assignment uses the first byte, matching PHP for a multi-byte value.\n\n## Verification\n\n- Focused P9 and required consumer namespaces run through the JVM AST-walker harness.\n- Kondo: 0 errors, 0 warnings on touched source and test files.\n- cljstyle: clean after formatting `scope.cljc` and `prelude_module.cljc`.\n- Parser classes were generated locally with `clj -M:antlr-gen`; generated outputs are not part of the commit.\n# xlang slice 2 findings\n\n## Implemented\n\n- Generalized `yang.call.conformance` with frontend profiles for TypeScript, PHP, and Python. Publication, runtime initialization, donor execution, export reads, caller projection, linking, and rendering all use the shared profile path.\n- Added Python <-> TypeScript and Python <-> PHP in both directions. Every new leg passes a callback into the foreign function, stores it, checks same-cell identity, calls it back, and asserts the result.\n- Python integer results are bigint values at the JavaScript boundary. The TypeScript leg converts explicitly with `Number`; the Python donor converts the TypeScript callback's integer result with `float` before adding a JavaScript-compatible number. PHP's integer path needs no conversion.\n- Python `print` caller sources include the parser-required final newline.\n\n## Named skip\n\n- `yang.clojure <-> TypeScript`, both directions: `yang.clojure` has convention-wired application lowering, but no published runtime module, `run-main` entry, or runtime global namespace through which the shared helper can execute a donor and project exports. Supporting these legs requires frontend/runtime work rather than a minimal test-helper generalization.\n\n## Gates\n\n- `clojure -M:test -n yang.cross-lang-test`: pending final run.\n- `clojure -M:kondo --lint test/yang/call/conformance.clj test/yang/cross_lang_test.clj`: 0 errors, 0 warnings.\n- `mise exec -- cljstyle check test/yang/call/conformance.clj test/yang/cross_lang_test.clj`: passed.\ncommit d01a7c80ae50216627fae6f8639a49a5b7c7eb66\nAuthor: Sonny To <son.c.to@gmail.com>\n\n    docs(ledger): the Linux datagram refusals-and-lifecycle rows close (a226423d) and dedupe 4 rows to 1\n\n docs/agents/known-gaps.md | 5 +----\n 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 4 deletions(-)\ncommit d01a7c80ae50216627fae6f8639a49a5b7c7eb66\nAuthor: Sonny To <son.c.to@gmail.com>\nDate:   Mon Nov 2 21:15:43 2026 +0700\n\n    docs(ledger): the Linux datagram refusals-and-lifecycle rows close (a226423d) and dedupe 4 rows to 1\n\ndiff --git a/docs/agents/known-gaps.md b/docs/agents/known-gaps.md\nindex b306a1c3..c0f6b2a3 100644\n--- a/docs/agents/known-gaps.md\n+++ b/docs/agents/known-gaps.md\n@@ -28,7 +28,7 @@ Adopted by the owner 2026-10-14 (mob consolidation Q6).\n | Historical citations of `docs/design/yin.vm.semantic.md` with v3 section numbers, now wrong after the rename and outside the nine-line allowance: `src/cljc/yin/vm.cljc:655` (§2), `src/cljc/datomworld/demo/continuation_handoff.cljc:67`, `src/cljs/datomworld/demo/continuation_stream.cljs:10` (§7), `src/cljd/yin/register_bench_cljd.cljd:6` (§8), `src/cljc/yin/vm/docs/jfr_benchmark_analysis.md:5,268` (§8), `test/bench/yin_vm_bench.cljc:3` (§8), `test/yin/repl_test.cljc:37` (§8), `test/yin/vm/semantic/linearize_test.cljc:286` (§2.7); in the renamed design §2 is the machine, §7 is \"What A is\", §8 is the derivations | 8g Architect review P2-1 | yin.vm.semantic (the register-VM track) | closed in follow-up-1: retargeted to the history block or current projection/cutover sections; only prose changed | P3 |\n | Historical source prose outside the nine citation-line allowance: the optimisation note mentions the deleted `vm/opcase`; `ucf/rows/checkpoint.cljc` says it replaces the now-deleted `yin.vm.ucf.checkpoint` | 8f-1 review D1 / P3-5 | yin.vm.semantic 