with string keys (`f(...['a' => 1])`) is refused at run time with `Error \"spread with string keys is not supported yet (yang.php known gap G-spread-string-keys)\"` (C25); PHP binds the keys as named arguments, so row 65 is not claimed at program level; fixture `:call-spread-string-key-gap` (oracle-only, pending the next shiva pass) | Stage 0 gate D2; `e2e-test/gate-fix-programs-test` | yang.php | P4 (row 65 lands with `pcall-arg-named`) | P2 |\n538:| yang.php: by-reference `foreach` keeps an ordinal and re-reads the location each iteration (C26, `G-foreach-iterator-registry`); the same-table clause of rows 25 and 26 is implemented, the copy-hit and unrelated clauses of row 25, the rebuild clause of row 26 and rows 54, 60 and 61 are not (`sort($a)` or `$a = [..]` inside the loop differ from PHP); `fe-next` is a linear scan per iteration; fixtures `:foreach-ref-sort-inside-loop` and `:foreach-ref-array-reassigned-in-loop` (oracle-only, pending) | Stage 0 gate D3; design 17.2 C26 | yang.php | P3-c (iterator registry, the P3 plan's S7.2 and S7.3), before P4-b lands row 29 | P2 |\n539:| yang.php: the vendored `PhpParser.g4` reads `fn($x)` as a call to a function named `fn` and `[fn($x) => ...]` as a key/value pair, and has no `foreach (... as $k => [$x, $y])`; the held fixtures `:call-dynamic-dim` and `:foreach-key-and-destructure` keep their recorded oracle values and flip on with a grammar patch (C27, `G-grammar-fn-item`) | Stage 0 gate D4; vendored grammar byte-identical to upstream `85e2dd17` | yang.php | a grammar-patch slice through the manifest `:patches` mechanism, regenerated on every target, before or inside P4 S0 | P2 |\n540:| yang.php: member calls go through one `php/method-call` seam (`getMessage`, `getCode`, `getPrevious` on Throwable; `bindTo`, `__invoke` on Closure); `bindTo` shares statics with the source closure (PHP copies them); `new` and classes are refused; the call protocol validates a named argument's name at entry, so in `f(1, z: 2, w: side())`