endent review (codex gpt-6.1-sol round 2, P2) and Architect sign-off condition 5; `src/cljc/yang/php/antlr/lower.cljc` parameter initialization | yang.php | P4 S6 (cover parameter initialization in the unwinding cleanup so every acquired parameter is released on failure) | P2 |\n571:| yang.php: a later rejected by-reference argument leaks an earlier parameter's acquisition: with `function f(D &$a, int &$b)`, `$a = new D`, `$b = 'bad'`, `catch (TypeError $e)`, then `$e = null; unset($a); echo 'E';`, PHP prints `cDE` (the freed trace releases its copy, `unset` drops the last holder) and yang.php prints `cED` (the acquisition of `$a` made before `$b` failed is never released, because cleanup surrounds only the body, not parameter initialization). Without `$e = null` both print `cED`, PHP because the trace holds the argument (corner C30), yang.php because of this leak | P4 S5 independent review (codex gpt-6.1-sol round 2, P2) and Architect sign-off condition 5, restated by the 17.3 ruling of 2026-10-28; `src/cljc/yang/php/antlr/lower.cljc` parameter initialization | yang.php | P4 S6 (cover parameter initialization in the unwinding cleanup so every acquired parameter is released on failure); fixture `:decl-byref-later-rejection-releases-earlier-param` (`#{:p4-s6}`) | P2 |\n572:| yang.php C30: exception traces hold no arguments, so an argument rejected at acquisition is released at the throw where PHP keeps it alive until the exception is freed (departure `cDE` vs `cED`) | 17.3 ruling 2026-10-28 on oracle pass 9; design section 17.2 C30 | yang.php | none scheduled; a trace-frames slice | P3 |\n573:| yang.php: compile-time default validation was incomplete (a float default for an `int` property or parameter, arrays and signed literals passed lowering, and `:unknown` escaped whenever a class, object, callable or iterable member existed); closed in P4 S6: `init-kind` classifies int, float, string, bool, null, array and signed numeric defaults from the syntax tree, `kind-fits