e rebinding does not warn for the unbind-`$this` and internal-class cases, and `static` is accepted only as a return type (as a parameter or property type it never matches) | P4 S6 | yang.php | P4 S10 (departure fixtures from the object permutation alphabet) | P3 |\n577:| yang.php: destructuring by reference into a property (`[&$o->p] = $a`, row 47) is not lowered: the destructuring pattern accepts variable and element targets only; fixture `:obj-row47-destructure-by-ref-into-typed-property` is authored and gated by `:p4-row47` | checkpoint B audit (fixture package); `src/cljc/yang/php/antlr/lower.cljc` `pattern-of` | yang.php | P4 S7 or a destructuring slice before checkpoint C (the gate lifts when the pattern accepts property targets) | P2 |\n578:| yang.php: `exit`/`die` is refused (`:constant`), so row 51 (`exit` inside a destructor proceeds to shutdown, corner C9) cannot run; fixture `:obj-row51-exit-in-destructor` is authored and gated by `:p4-exit` | checkpoint B audit (fixture package); design row 51 | yang.php | P4 S7 (the exit escape and the pending-exception destruct halt) | P2 |\n579:| yang.php: a direct write to a typed static property (`A::$s = 'x'`) is not type-checked; only a reference to it is (a source keyed by class and property, row 46), so assignment through the reference is checked and the direct assignment is not | checkpoint B audit (fixture package) | yang.php | P4 S10 (departure fixture from the object permutation alphabet) or earlier if the sprop write path gains a coercion | P3 |\n580:| yang.php C37: `__FILE__`/`__DIR__` use the unit's declared relative path (`.` for a root unit), not absolute filesystem paths; fixture `:const-file-dir-raw` records the departure and oracle comparison normalizes `/w/<id>` to `.` | P6 plan v2 R2, design 17.2 C37 | yang.php | retained as a P6 departure | P3 |\n581:| yang.php C38: folded include paths resolve at the composition root; PHP's including-script directory and additional `include_path` searches are n