tract instantiation) are `Error`\n  throws. The uncaught-exception text is pinned to PHP's `PHP Fatal error:\n  Uncaught ...` format without the file path.\n\n### 3.10 Generators and iteration protocols\n|    |                                    | exhaustion, cancellation) skip the |\n|    |                                    | destructor phase, as Zend skips it |\n|    |                                    | on fatal errors                    |\n+----+------------------------------------+------------------------------------+\n\n### 4.5 Oracle facts and anchor programs\n\nThree outputs were obtained first-hand from PHP 8.3 (image `php:8.3-cli`, host\nshiva, 2026-10-17) and are the fixture group `oracle-2026-10-17`, recorded\nwith that provenance:\n\n- **F1** (copy lineage, rows 25 and 60): `$a=[10,20,30]; foreach ($a as &$v) {\n  echo \"$v,\"; if (first) { $b=$a; $a[2]=99; } }` prints `10,20,99,`.\n- **F2** (named arguments, row 57): with `function f($x) {}` and a `side()`\n  that echoes `late`, `f(bad: 1, x: side())` raises `Error: Unknown named\n  parameter $bad`, and `late` is never printed. `f(bad: side())` runs `side()`\n  and then raises the same `Error`.\n- **F3** (readonly clone, rows 66 and 67): with `public readonly int $x`\n  initialized to 1 in the constructor, `function __clone() { unset($this->x);\n  $this->x = 2; }` yields `2` with no error.\n\nThe oracle harness strips an uncaught-`Throwable` or plain-fatal block from\nthe captured stdout and reports it as the program's `:uncaught` result. The\nstrip ends at the block's own terminator (`thrown in FILE on line N` for an\nuncaught throwable, the `on line N` message end for a plain fatal), so output\nwritten afterwards (shutdown functions and destructors of row 22) stays in\n`:out`.\n\nAnchor programs that every revision of the table has been traced against\n(expected PHP 8.3 output):\n\n+--------------------------------------+---------------------------------------+\n| Program                              | Output                                |\n+======================================+=======================================+\n| `$a=[1]; $r=&$a[0]; $b=$a; $b[0]=2;  | `2`                                   |\n| echo $a[0];`                         |                                       |\n+--------------------------------------+---------------------------------------+\n| `$a=[1]; $r=&$a[0]; unset($r);       | `1`                                   |\n| $b=$a; $b[0]=2; echo $a[0];`         |                                       |\nzsh:1: no matches found: test/yang/php/antlr/oracle*\ntest/yang/latte_oracle/kernel_gate.edn\ntest/yang/latte_oracle/slice8_sequences.edn\ntest/yang/latte_oracle/context.edn\ntest/yang/latte_oracle/slice7_anchors.edn\ntest/yang/latte_oracle/slice9_evidence.edn\ntest/yang/latte_oracle/slice8_evidence.edn\ntest/yang/latte_oracle/unfold_implicit.edn\ntest/yang/latte_oracle/case_arms.edn\ntest/yang/latte_oracle/throw_sites.edn\ntest/yang/latte_oracle/slice9_unexercised.edn\ntest/yang/latte_oracle/fixture_closure.edn\ntest/yang/latte_oracle/slice9_verification.edn\ntest/yang/latte_oracle/slice9_declarations.edn\ntest/yang/latte_oracle/manifest.edn\ntest/resources/dao/space/datomic-q-v1.oracle-observations.edn\ntest/resources/yang/typescript/t3_oracle.edn\ntest/resources/yang/typescript/t1_oracle.edn\ntest/resources/yang/typescript/t2_oracle.edn\ntest/yang/python/antlr/fixtures/jolt_j0c_input_oracle.edn\ntest/yang/python/antlr/fixtures/jolt_j0c_oracle.edn\n   820\t      (reduce (fn [acc piece] (app* 'php/concat acc piece)) pieces))))\n   821\t\n   822\t\n   823\t(defn- string-node\n   824\t  \"The node of a `string` rule: single and double quoted literals; a\n   825\t   double-quoted string interpolates plain scalar variables only (`$x`,\n   826\t   `{$x}`; indexes, properties and `${}` are P2/P4).\"\n   827\t  [ctx n]\n   828\t  (let [ks (core/kids ctx n)\n   829\t        k0 (first ks)]\n   830\t    (case (:type k0)\n   831\t      \"SingleQuot