{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_42","type":"agent_message","text":"I found two substantive problems in the fatal and exit paths. Budget exhaustion runs cleanup thunks that can invoke destructors or replace the fatal, and `exit` uses exception unwinding, which runs guest `finally` blocks. P9 also has nonterminating cases for empty replacement needles and zero range steps, plus fixtures that omit PHP warnings."}}
