admitted\"\n   105\t          (xl/call [:clojure \"(defn clj-apply [f] (+ (f 20) 1))\"]\n   106\t                   [\"clj_apply\"]\n   107\t                   [:typescript \"console.log(clj_apply);\"])))))\n   108\t\n   109\t\n   202\t(defn compose\n   203\t  \"The caller program: the donor's body run, each name of `exports` read\n   204\t   from the donor runtime and projected into `caller-frontend`'s namespace\n   205\t   under the same name, then `caller-source`, lowered unmodified, run under\n   206\t   its runtime's entry. Its value is the caller entry's value.\"\n   207\t  [donor exports caller-frontend caller-source]\n   208\t  (let [{:keys [read-export]} (profile (:frontend donor))\n   209\t        {:keys [project parse unit run-main]} (profile caller-frontend)]\n   210\t    (u/mark-tails\n   211\t      (u/seq-nodes\n   212\t        (concat (runtime-entry [(:frontend donor) caller-frontend])\n   213\t                (donor-run donor)\n   214\t                (map (fn [export]\n   215\t                       (let [value (symbol (str \"xlang.export.\" export))]\n   216\t                         (u/let1 value\n   217\t                                 (u/sexp->uast (read-export export))\n   218\t                                 (u/sexp->uast (project export value)))))\n   219\t                     exports)\n   220\t                [(u/app (u/v run-main) (unit (parse caller-source) exports))])))))\n   221\t\n   222\t\n  3972\t\n  3973\tThe current code records the gap, not a second normative convention:\n  3974\t\n  3975\t| Current implementation | Private call path |\n  3976\t|---|---|\n  3977\t| `yang.python.antlr.prelude` | `py/call-kw` binds arguments and applies the function cell's `:code` to one vector. |\n  3978\t| `yang.typescript.antlr.prelude` | `js/call` checks `:js/type :function` and applies `:code` to receiver and argument vector. |\n  3979\t| `yang.php.antlr.prelude` | `php/call` applies `:code` to the function cell and argument vector; named/reference handling is separate. |\n  3980\t| `test/yang/cross_lang_test.clj` | Demonstrates PHP/TypeScript substrate composition using lookup rewriting and a test-local `js-shaped` wrapper; not proof of this convention. |\n  3981\t\n  3982\tImplementation proceeds as separately verified changes:\n  3983\t\n  3984\t1. Supply the shared guest prelude and fixtures for entry discovery,\n M orchestrator-logs/1793292851-yang-python-retake.md\n?? .flutter-plugins-dependencies\n?? collab/1793546000000-engineer-node-shard-uncovered-skip.kimi-k3.1-pro.findings.md\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
